  (38, 6, $svjson${"evidence":{"limitation":"Complete all required fields before submitting. Version 3 (CERT-REFINE-01) adds the certificate QA refinement data slots. Version 4 (QAFIX-01) enters the application purpose once with a language choice, seats Bangla/English companion fields beside each other, unifies the document-language label and applies the live-QA spelling corrections. Version 5 (QAFIX-08) states who the application is for (with the subject's name when it is for someone else), grades the disability's severity on a fixed scale, captures the diagnosed condition in both languages, makes the English support-needs field required like its Bangla original, and makes the documents step name the medical/disability certificate and require at least one upload. The certificate prints the disability type and the support needs only, so the relation, subject, severity and diagnosis are office evidence. Version 6 (QAFIX-10) seats the English description beside its Bangla pair: both halves are now text fields, because the form grid spans every textarea across the full row, so no textarea pair can sit side by side. Labels and limits are unchanged, and the issuance gate still sees both halves required. The pair is also seated in one grid row by moving disability_severity to just after the English half — a pair starting in the second column straddles the row boundary, so the type change alone does not seat it.","source":"audit/evidence/s-38.json","status":"proposed"},"sections":[{"fields":[{"constraints":{"required":true},"evidence":{"status":"proposed"},"id":"disability_applicant_relation","label":{"bn":"কার জন্য আবেদন করছেন","en":"Who is this application for"},"options":[{"label":{"bn":"নিজের জন্য (আমি নিজে প্রতিবন্ধী ব্যক্তি)","en":"For myself (I am the person with a disability)"},"value":"self"},{"label":{"bn":"অন্য প্রতিবন্ধী ব্যক্তির পক্ষে","en":"For another person with a disability"},"value":"other"}],"type":"select"},{"constraints":{"maxLength":160,"required":tru